# Mistakes: texts that do not compile, on any database, each error at its place.

=== = in a condition
from cases
where status = "open"
--- error
2:14 use `==` to compare

=== a step that does not exist
from cases
wehre risk > 90
--- error
2:1 there is no step `wehre`

=== a column that does not exist
from cases
where stauts == "open"
--- error
2:7 there is no column `stauts` in `cases`

=== a table that does not exist
from casse
--- error
1:6 there is no table `casse`

=== a function that does not exist
from cases
select n = lenght(key)
--- error
2:12 there is no function `lenght`

=== a query has one from
from cases
from accounts
--- error
2:1 a query has one `from`

=== two columns of the same name
from cases
select key, key = risk
--- error
2:13 there are two columns named `key`

=== after a change, only a select can follow
from cases
delete
sort key
--- error
3:1 after a change, only a `select` can follow

=== only where chooses the rows to change
from cases
sort -risk
update status = "urgent"
--- error
2:1 only `where` can choose the rows to update

=== the queries combined have different columns
both = (from cases; select key) + (from accounts; select id)

from both
--- error
1:35 the queries have different columns

=== every row written in a query has the same columns
from [{"id": "A9", "operator": "X"}, {"id": "A8"}]
insert into accounts
--- error
1:38 every row has the same columns
